Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: use list membership for failed link cleanup

hostapd_setup_bss() sets started before adding the link to the driver.
If link_add fails while another link exists, the old started/first-BSS
checks reach dl_list_del() with a zeroed link node and crash hostapd.
Conversely, a link registered during driver_init() still needs unlinking
after its driver private data has been cleared.

Use actual list membership instead of the BSS setup state, and make
hostapd_mld_remove_link() safe for a never-added or already-removed link.

--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -728,21 +728,8 @@ void hostapd_bss_link_deinit(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 	}
 
 	/* Put all freeing logic above this */
-	if (!hapd->mld || !hapd->mld->num_links)
-		return;
-
-	/* If not started, not yet linked to the MLD. However, the first
-	 * BSS is always linked since it is linked during driver_init(), and
-	 * hence, need to remove it from the AP MLD.
-	 */
-	if (!hapd->started && hapd->iface->bss[0] != hapd)
-		return;
-
-	/* The first BSS can also be only linked when at least driver_init() is
-	 * executed. But if previous interface fails, it is not, and hence,
-	 * safe to skip.
-	 */
-	if (hapd->iface->bss[0] == hapd && !hapd->drv_priv)
+	/* started is set before link_add, so it is not proof of membership. */
+	if (!hapd->mld || !hapd->link.next)
 		return;
 
 	hostapd_mld_remove_link(hapd);
@@ -5387,6 +5374,9 @@ int hostapd_mld_remove_link(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 	if (!mld)
 		return -1;
 
+	if (!hapd->link.next)
+		return 0;
+
 	dl_list_del(&hapd->link);
 	mld->num_links--;
 
